# TUI keybinding conventions

Curators move through epublate fast — flagged segment in the Inbox,
Reader to fix it, back to Glossary to lock the entry, Dashboard to
re-batch. Every keystroke that means "the same thing on a different
screen" must use the same key. Inconsistencies (Enter submits here
but not there; `r` refreshes here but retries there) burn 5 seconds
of cognitive load each — fast enough to ruin the workflow. These
rules codify what's been observed to work and what's been seen to
break.

## View screens (Dashboard, Inbox, Glossary, LLM Activity, Logs, Lore Books, Intake history, …)

Read-only or list-style surfaces where the curator scans, picks, and
opens detail screens.

| Key      | Action  | Notes                                              |
| -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| `Enter`  | Open selected row / primary action | Routes via `DataTable.RowSelected` when applicable |
| `r`      | Refresh | Re-poll the DB and repaint                         |
| `f`      | Cycle filter | When the screen has a stream of mixed kinds   |
| `q`      | Back    | Pop screen                                         |
| `Esc`    | Back    | Mirror of `q`, hidden from footer to keep it short |
| `?` / `F1` | Help  | App-level binding, always available                |
| `T`      | Cycle theme | App-level binding                              |

The Dashboard exposes uppercase `I` for the Intake history screen
(lowercase `i` already routes to the Inbox); the
`IntakeRunDetailModal` uses `s` to apply the helper-suggested tone
and `g` to jump to the Glossary screen.

## Form modals (`BatchModal`, `BudgetModal`, `IntakeModal`, `EntryEditScreen`, `LoreIngestModal`, `NewProjectModal`, `OpenProjectModal`, `ExportModal`, `LoreImportProjectModal`, `NewLoreBookModal`, `OpenLoreBookModal`, …)

Editable forms with one or more `Input` / `Select` widgets. The
curator should be able to:

| Key       | Action |
| --------- | ------ |
| `Enter`   | Submit (works from any single-line `Input`) |
| `Ctrl+S`  | Submit (works anywhere, including `TextArea`) |
| `Esc`     | Cancel and dismiss with `None` |

Implementation contract for every form modal:

1. Bind `ctrl+s` to `action_submit` (or `action_save`).
2. Bind `escape` to `action_cancel`.
3. Override `on_input_submitted(self, event: Input.Submitted)` to
   call `self.action_submit()` (or `action_save`). This is the
   piece that's been missing on multiple modals — when the curator
   types a value and hits Enter, nothing happens and they have to
   reach for Ctrl+S.
4. The footer hint string must read `"Press Enter or Ctrl+S to
   <verb>, Esc to cancel."` so the convention is discoverable
   in-modal.

```python
# ✅ GOOD — every form modal carries this pair
def on_input_submitted(self, event: Input.Submitted) -> None:
    del event
    self.action_submit()

def action_submit(self) -> None:
    ...
```

```python
# ❌ BAD — only Ctrl+S works; Enter on the Input does nothing
def action_submit(self) -> None:
    ...
```

## Yes/No confirm modals (`CascadeConfirmScreen`, `MergeDuplicatesScreen`, `DeleteConfirmScreen`, `RemoveRecentConfirmModal`, `LoreConflictResolveModal`, …)

| Key   | Action |
| ----- | ------ |
| `y`   | Confirm |
| `n`   | Cancel |
| `Esc` | Cancel |

Don't add `Enter` on these — they have no input field and no
unambiguous "primary action" to submit. The two-letter `y`/`n`
discipline is what makes them safe.

## Editor screens (Reader, `EditTargetScreen`)

The Reader and the in-segment edit modal are deliberate exceptions.

| Key       | Reader meaning | Notes |
| --------- | -------------- | ----- |
| `r`       | **Retry** (re-translate current segment) | Conflicts with view `r` = Refresh; Reader is an editor, not a view |
| `t`       | Translate next | |
| `b`       | Translate chapter | |
| `a` / `A` | Accept / Approve chapter | |
| `e`       | Edit (push `EditTargetScreen`) | |
| arrows    | Move segment / chapter focus | |
| `Ctrl+S`  | (in `EditTargetScreen`) Save the target | `Enter` is content (multi-line); only `Ctrl+S` saves |
| `Esc`     | Cancel / back | |

The `r` conflict is explicit and intentional: the Reader has no
"refresh from DB" semantics (it lives off the stats poller), and
"retry the LLM call" is the most-used action there. Document this
in code comments rather than remap.

## Don't

- Don't introduce a key that means a different verb on a different
  screen unless it's documented as an editor exception above.
- Don't add `Enter`-to-submit only on some form modals. Either every
  form modal supports it, or none do. (The standard is "every".)
- Don't bury submit/cancel hints — every form modal must show the
  footer hint string. Curators don't memorize 12 modals' bindings.
- Don't rely on screen order. The slim `BatchStatusBar` may be
  docked between content and `Footer`; never assume the Footer is
  the only bottom-docked widget on a screen.
